  "question": {
    "text": "Which one of the following does not have a pyramidal shape?"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "\n$\\left(\\mathrm{CH}_3\\right)_3 \\mathrm{~N}$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$\\left(\\mathrm{SiH}_3\\right)_3 \\mathrm{~N}$\n",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{P}\\left(\\mathrm{CH}_3\\right)_3$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{P}\\left(\\mathrm{SiH}_3\\right)_3$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "In case of $\\mathrm{N}\\left(\\mathrm{SiH}_3\\right)_3 \\mathrm{~N}$ atom is $s p^2$ hybridised, the lone pair is present in $2 p$ orbital and it is transferred to empty $d$ orbital of Si forming $d \\pi-p \\pi$ bond. Hence nitrogen with $s p^2$ hybridization has trigonal planar shape."
  }
}